      "title": "Find the coefficient in one summand",
      "body": "Think of a power of the bracket as a product of identical brackets. A linear term is formed by selecting x from one bracket and constants from the others.",
      "recap": "Coefficients of the same power add when polynomial expressions are added.",
      "pitfall": "Handle the zero-power summand separately.",
      "pause": "Derive the linear coefficient for a general exponent, then list the coefficients needed in this sum.",
      "recall": [
